<!--
  Consistency: Mucousy — two slanted streaks, a jelly rather than a lump.

  REDRAWN after the owner read the first version on the phone and asked what the letter T was doing in
  the consistency row. It was: a wide bar across the top, a stem below it, and a dot under that — a T
  with a tail, at 16dp, next to six shapes that all read as forms.

  The idea worth keeping was "it SLIDES rather than sits", so the new drawing says that with two
  streaks at the same angle and different lengths, which is what stringy stool looks like and what
  nothing else in the set does. Diarrhea keeps the droplets above a spreading pool; Runny keeps the
  mass over a wide pool; neither has a streak.
-->
